 "notes": "Paper reports two distinct exclusion limits from two separate measurement runs: (1) ALP (AxionPhoton) limit at m_a = 7.2 \u00b5eV with g = 4.5\u00d710^-8 GeV^-1 from June 2013 run in 3T magnet; (2) HSP (DarkPhoton) limit at m_\u03b3' = 10.8 \u00b5eV with \u03c7 = 4.1\u00d710^-9 from September 2013 run. The paper uses a microwave light-shining-through-wall (LSW) setup. For ALPs, the coupling is to photons via the Primakoff effect (g_agamma in GeV^-1). For HSPs, the coupling is kinetic mixing (\u03c7, dimensionless). Since the abstract and main results emphasize both particle types equally and the paper presents two separate exclusion plots (Figs. 13 and 14), this represents a MIXED coupling-type result. However, the pre-analysis hint and the prominence of the ALP result in the abstract suggest AxionPhoton as primary. The HSP result (DarkPhoton) is also clearly stated but secondary. Confidence is moderate (0.75) because the paper constrains TWO distinct coupling types with different conventions, requiring careful disambiguation. Both limits are at 95% CL. No local DM density assumption applies (this is a laboratory LSW experiment, not a haloscope). | vector-trace candidate: HSP_excl_plot.pdf colour (0.0, 0.0, 0.0), 106 pts (selected among 3) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 106))",
